<title>AUSTRIA: EVN knocked down by disappointing H1.</title>
<headline>EVN knocked down by disappointing H1.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in regional utility company EVN traded lower in an overall buoyant market on Tuesday on what traders attributed to disappointment over the firm's batch of weaker first-half earnings.</p>
<p>EVN said pretax profit in the first half to February sagged 14.1 percent to 1.621 billion schillings and operating profit fell 17.4 percent to 1.43 billion schillings.</p>
<p>At 0750 GMT, EVN was down 1.81 percent, or 29 schillings, at 1,570 while the blue-chip ATX index was 0.5 percent higher. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
</text>
